# Copy to ~/.grimnir/hygiene-allow-words.txt (or set $GRIMNIR_HYGIENE_ALLOW_WORDS).
#
# scripts/check-repo-hygiene.sh derives program-name patterns from the directory
# names under your workspace ($GRIMNIR_WORKSPACE, default ~/workspace), so a new
# engagement is covered the moment its directory exists and nobody has to
# remember to add it. The cost of deriving is false positives: a handle that is
# also an ordinary word, or a vendor whose name is a legitimate fingerprinting
# category, looks identical to a leak from a regex's point of view.
#
# List those here, one per line, case-insensitive. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored.
#
# This file is operator-local and never committed, for the same reason the
# pattern file is: a tracked list of which words to ignore would itself be a
# list of the programs you work on.
#
# CLAUDE.md permits generic vendor names used as fingerprinting categories
# (CMS, chat widgets, cloud providers) in tracked files. Those are the usual
# entries here. Add a word only after checking that its tracked occurrences are
# genuinely generic; when in doubt, leave it out and let the gate block.
#
# Illustrative entries — replace with your own:
#
# acme                 # handle that is also an ordinary word
# examplecrm           # vendor named as a recon fingerprint, not a target
# cloudvendor          # cloud provider named as a metadata-endpoint category
